      "side": 1,
      "message": "I expanded the commit message to explain the motivation.\n\nThis is split out as a small leaf prerequisite for change 630421, which uses it to encrypt stored OAuth token fields. The reusable part is not OAuth-specific: AES-GCM seal/open, random IVs, AAD binding, envelope parsing, and HKDF-SHA256 key derivation.\n\nThe OAuth change then owns only the OAuth policy: which fields are encrypted, which values are bound as AAD, and how legacy cleartext entries are handled.\n\nIt still uses only JDK/JCE primitives. The only local crypto composition is HKDF-SHA256, because Gerrit still supports Java 21 and the JDK HKDF API is newer.",
